  [34mdescription:[0m  During bd-757d87 landing prep, operator guidance required frequent first-party rebases plus local backup branches. The recorded summary template asks for commit SHAs, but after each rebase the code and summary commits changed, making summary.md stale until manually edited/amended. This is easy to miss before recorded reintegration and adds friction to safe frequent rebasing. Suggested fix: provide a first-party summary refresh/check helper that detects stale commit references after rebase, or prefer stable bead/branch references plus automatically injected final landed commit metadata in recorded summaries. Filed via reflect-session mixin from bd-757d87 session.
